<title>DENMARK: Danish Wise Men raise GDP growth forecasts.</title>
<headline>Danish Wise Men raise GDP growth forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The independent Danish Economic Council said in its biannual report on Wednesday that it expected 2.0 percent growth in Gross Domestic Product (GDP) in 1996 and 2.9 percent in 1997.</p>
<p>In its previous report last May, the council, known as the Wise Men, predicted 1996 growth of 0.9 percent and 1997 growth of 2.2 percent.</p>
<p>--Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33 969650</p>
</text>
